{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Brave New World of the Internet"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Do I Do?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Explain about technology and technical problems in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes an exchange of written communications about asking for and giving advice on problems with technology or gadgets through the correct use of spelling, grammar, vocabulary, level of formality, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriated to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le10ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Dealing With Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are several ways to ask for help with a technical problem in English. You can use polite and casual language to do this. You can also use questions within sentences to ask for clarification.<br/><br/>One way to discuss how to deal with problems is to say what you would do if you were in someone else's situation. It is particularly useful if you want to discuss a complicated technical problem."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to ask for help, you can use the structure:<br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Can</span>/ <span class=\"strong\">Could</span>/ <span class=\"strong\">Do</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">you</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">verb</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">me (optional)</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">Question word</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"italic\">Can you show me how this computer works?<br/> Could you tell me where I can find reliable information?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also suggest advice by using the same structure:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Do you know where to go online for the best information?<br/> Do you know what to look for when you check a website's accuracy?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to offer advice and suggestions on how to solve technical issues, you can use modals like  <span class=\"italic\">would</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or  <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to suggest solutions and offer assistance. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I would ... <br/> I wouldn't ...<br/> You could ... </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can also use must, might want to  or Imperatives to strongly suggest a solution."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"italic\">You might want to ...<br/> You must ... <br/> Always check ...</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Asking for Help\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Offering Advice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you tell me how to get started?<br/>  Do you think that I can meet my next girlfriend through a search engine?<br/>  Do you know how hard it is to meet someone in this town? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I think you should try meeting people online. <br/>  Well, make sure that your social media pages are up-to-date.<br/>  I have a few tips that may help you.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking About the Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>When you talk about a things that are not decided or when you  make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use  the modal <span class=\"italic\">will.</li>  <li>When you ask about intentions, you use  <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>.</li>  <li>When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda  or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.</li>  <li>When you talk about schedules or timetables  in the future, you use the Simple Present tense.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Verb Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Future Tense (Will)</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Ok. I'll do that this weekend.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You're not going to meet anyone with a profile that is out of date!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I'm finishing a feature on new technologies for the magazine later.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There's a singles night nearby next Tuesday. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Virtual Reality"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a computer-generated simulation of real life that a user can interact with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: With Virtual Reality, you're going to have experiences you can't have in the real world."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "advocate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person who strongly supports a cause or an idea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I just had the most amazing interview with a technology advocate"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "digital native "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who has used the Internet from an early age"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's impossible to remember life before the Internet if you are a digital native."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "up-to-date"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "containing the latest information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Not everything you read online is up-to-date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "out of date"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "no longer valid or relevant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will find websites that are simply out of date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "user-friendly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "easy to use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You might want to check that the website is user-friendly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le10ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "search engine"}, {"type": "definition", "conte